  ./presswarden cleanup [target]       Logs + disposable metadata/inode cleanup
  ./presswarden doctor [target]        Dependencies, config, integrations, discovery
  ./presswarden last-run               Show the most recently started suite run state
  ./presswarden run-status [RUN_ID]    Show latest or a specific suite run state
  ./presswarden history [RUN_ID]       Show NEW/RECURRING/CHANGED/RESOLVED/NOT RECHECKED findings
  ./presswarden continue [RUN_ID]      Safely continue an interrupted suite from its first unfinished check
  ./presswarden lock [target]          Lock WordPress file modifications across discovered sites
  ./presswarden unlock [target]        Unlock WordPress file modifications for updates/maintenance
  ./presswarden lock-status [target]   Show DISALLOW_FILE_MODS status across discovered sites
  ./presswarden auto-updates status [target]  Show core/plugin/theme auto-update policy
  ./presswarden auto-updates core minor|major|disabled [target]
  ./presswarden auto-updates plugins enable|disable [target]
  ./presswarden auto-updates themes enable|disable [target]
  ./presswarden wp-settings [target]       WordPress policy dashboard / fleet baseline differences
  ./presswarden wp-settings set SETTING VALUE [target]  Change supported wp-config policy
  ./presswarden file-mods ACTION [target]  Legacy/advanced status|on|off interface
  ./presswarden config               Show sanitized effective configuration
  ./presswarden config-new           List template options absent from saved config
  ./presswarden sites [path]         List local website names and directories
  ./presswarden --version
  ./presswarden help

Installed user-wide? The same commands also work as: presswarden fast, presswarden full, etc.
